data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"`det(A) = sign * product(pivots)`. For each column, choose the largest-magnitude entry on or below\nthe diagonal, swap it into place (flipping the sign if the row changed), multiply the pivot into the\nproduct, and subtract multiples of the pivot row from the rows below. If the best pivot is exactly\nzero, the matrix is singular and the determinant is 0."},"hints_note":null}

